---
description: Shell — balanced quotes; avoid PS2 (dquote>, quote>, bquote>)
globs:
  - "**/*"
alwaysApply: true
message: |
  ## Shell

  **Default:** one logical command per line; no trailing `\`, `|`, `&&`, or unmatched `(` / `{` / `[` at EOL.

  **Quoting:** Even `"` and `'` counts outside the other style; close backticks and `$(`; prefer `printf '%s\n' 'literal'` over fragile `echo`.

  **Multi-line:** `cat <<'EOF' > file` with single-quoted delimiter; close delimiter on its own line.

  **Fenced blocks:** ```bash … ```; no `$` prompts in paste commands.

  **PS2 (`dquote>` / `quote>` / `bquote>`):** Ctrl-C; `stty sane; reset || true`; re-emit one balanced line.
